{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156337-travelling-to-the-abyss-it-is-possible","id":1156337,"title":"Travelling to the Abyss. It is possible?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-06T07:26:12-08:00","id":1156337,"title":"Travelling to the Abyss. It is possible?","content":"Hi, <br /> I have a question. Is it possible for Mage to travel into Abyss?<br /> <br /> For clarification I mean Abyss from Demon: The Fallen not Abyss Realm in middle umbra. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5536-arkilijo","name":"Arkilijo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T07:42:54-08:00","id":1156344,"title":"","content":"Go to the Shadowlands, enter the Labyrinth, don't get killed by hordes of Specters, follow it to the bottom, don't fall into Oblivion. Demon Abyss should be somewhere around there.<br /> <br /> There's no mention about Demon Abyss im Mage that I'm aware off. Maybe in Devils Due...but I don't remember anything about traveling there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T15:55:25-08:00","id":1156506,"title":"","content":"There is no clarification anywhere about what the Abyss of Demon resides in comparison to everything else known about the Umbra. Actually, it isn't even clear if the several Abyss-named realms are really several distinct realms, linked somehow, or actually the same saw by distinct parties.<br /> <br /> In the end, the answer is yes. From a MTA standpoint, there is no place you can't go with the right magic and a degree of effort. But the practicality of it depends on a lot of questions that the ST will have to answer alone.<br /> <br /> Some options: you can try to access it through Middle Umbra Abyss. That would need you to find some way to brace yourself against both the undoing effect of the place and its depressive effect. I guess that you got reasonable chances with Prime, Spirit, Life and Mind. It would be, of course, a guess try, very dangerous and without guarantees.<br /> <br /> You can try to go through Obtenebration's Abyss. To find how to access the damn place would be another thing entirely, but you probably can do if you put your hands over a high level user of Obtenebration and lets it experiment with the damn thing. In this case, what is highly dangerous and hard to pull is to find this Abyss, the actual journey can still be ripe on dangers, but nothing as the insta-kill of the previous expedition.<br /> <br /> As already presented, you can try the Labyrinth. It is probably the most dangerous of the three. But you can run out of options.<br /> <br /> Finally, all of those can be false paths, and the true one be something else entirely not yet known. Judging by the descriptions of the Demons, though, I assume that it is a place that can't attain visual representation, a realm of minds without the facsimile of space and matter that most realms have. So it could be either a very alien realm in the far reaches of the Umbra, or it could simply be a truly inconspicuous piece of the Astral Umbra, even one very near to Earth.<br /> <br /> Without a clear entrance, you can try to make amends with Correspondence. Coupled with Spirit and enough ranks, you can trace your way there by some other means. You could try to use the Correspondent link between another Abyss and &quot;true Hell&quot; to force one of the first trips to actually work in a way. You could use it on a Demon to trace it back to Hell, this would probably be the simplest way to find the Abyss' location, though it wouldn't necessarily give you means to reach it.<br /> <br /> Of course, all of that isn't enough to answer the final two questions: what would you find nearing the Abyss, and what effects you presence there would have on you. Whatever the Creator placed at the boundaries of Hell could keep Magi from entering it for all of Creation's history until now, as far as we know. And the &quot;place&quot; itself isn't meant for the presence of any other kind of being aside from Angels. Not even other spirits can dwell there, and it don't have space, time or matter references not even as an impression, distinguishing it from the rest of the known Umbra.<br /> <br /> Good luck on the trip.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T22:41:17-08:00","id":1156583,"title":"","content":"That plenty of good information. Thank you both.<br /> I was expecting something alongside it is not very feasible but technically possible. Now I know even some of horrors you can encounter be the way.<br /> <br /> But then another question rise if i may.<br /> <br /> What about all those infernal vampire (Baali), nephandi and another similar beast which presumably opens gates to the hell full of demons. It is some kind of another hell or what it is then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5536-arkilijo","name":"Arkilijo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T05:28:12-08:00","id":1156641,"title":"","content":"It can either be, be not, or exist both.<br /> <br /> The books never went clear on what infernalists were actually dealing with, much less if they were dealing with the same beings all the time. Instead, you have only in-character descriptions, and those are non-reliable.<br /> <br /> As a whole, the Umbra have at least half a dozen distinct ways of generating spirits that can be dubbed &quot;demons&quot;, and realms that can be described as hell. So probably most infernalists are not actually dealing with the Fallen, but with other kinds of demons (no less demonic). Some could be dealing with the Fallen, but on the course of history it probably wasn't all that common.<br /> <br /> Even then, Devil's Due demonstrates this point. Demons had been reaching Earth since dawn of civilization, so some are indeed Thralls. But the powers of those groups and their ritae and beliefs preclude the Fallen, and can work perfectly well with several other things. If you put Fallen in their midst, it is more probable that some will be Demon Thralls, either by the rules on DTF or DD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T10:08:54-08:00","id":1160895,"title":"","content":"The complexity of the answers to the &quot;Abyss&quot; and &quot;demon&quot; question can be illuminated by looking at the Wikia page for each. Abyss gives four options in the cWoD and Demon seven (considering the Fractured Cosmos model as canon). From a storytelling perspective, if there was a reason a character needed to go to DtF Abyss it seems the character would need to either go along for the ride, or be in some way become divine (the avatar goes and the player stays behind). If someone just wanted to go there, I'd have a hard time allowing a system that would.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T12:25:49-08:00","id":1160937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156337-travelling-to-the-abyss-it-is-possible?p=1156344#post1156344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go to the Shadowlands, enter the Labyrinth, don't get killed by hordes of Specters, follow it to the bottom, don't fall into Oblivion. Demon Abyss should be somewhere around there.<br /> <br /> There's no mention about Demon Abyss im Mage that I'm aware off. Maybe in Devils Due...but I don't remember anything about traveling there.</div> </div> </div> </div>you're missing the point.. oblivion IS the abyss. implied(and outright stated) to be so in quite a few sources. it's also the abyss of the lasombra. the abyss of werewolf is another entrance point. so is the well of souls( at least i think it's called such in the astral umbra) etc surviving there should probably be a spirit 5 feat though a specific rote would need to be researched.... for god's sake do NOT botch!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T15:18:16-08:00","id":1160982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156337-travelling-to-the-abyss-it-is-possible?p=1160937#post1160937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you're missing the point.. oblivion IS the abyss. implied(and outright stated) to be so in quite a few sources. it's also the abyss of the lasombra. the abyss of werewolf is another entrance point. so is the well of souls( at least i think it's called such in the astral umbra) etc surviving there should probably be a spirit 5 feat though a specific rote would need to be researched.... for god's sake do NOT botch!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious about the source. I personally never saw anything confirming this, though it does make sense in several ways. But canonical confirmation, or even it being implied, nothing that recall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T19:56:33-08:00","id":1161052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156337-travelling-to-the-abyss-it-is-possible?p=1160982#post1160982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious about the source. I personally never saw anything confirming this, though it does make sense in several ways. But canonical confirmation, or even it being implied, nothing that recall.</div> </div> </div> </div>to quote player's guide to the high clans &quot;ghosts rightly fear its hunger but do not understand it, demons call it hell and they only begin to comprehend&quot; also the labyrinth is said to be the other side of demons prison, book of worlds implies that oblivion lies beneath everything.<br /> other than that it's basic wod metaphysics and common sense. if they're all called ducks and they all behave like ducks and look like ducks.. they're ducks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T22:21:43-08:00","id":1161091,"title":"","content":"Vampire melds quite well with the Demon: the Fallen setting because of the common Christian theme, so I'd assume that the Baali hell <i>is </i>the DtF hell.<br /> <br /> Mages do summon some demons from somewhere and especially the Order of Hermes have quite the story about infernalism, but it's unclear whether the place is Malfeas or not. Still, Malfeas is a Middle Umbra realm so I'd call it the closest manifestation of Hell, but not really where the true devils are locked in; I think that a True Hell would be in the Deep Umbra, at the very least.<br /> <br /> That said, Mages are probably able to travel there <i>somehow</i>. But the &quot;how&quot; may very well require Spirit or Forces 9 and enough power to shatter God's will and rewrite the rules of the whole circle of reincarnation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 11-21-2017, 01:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T06:35:33-08:00","id":1161147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156337-travelling-to-the-abyss-it-is-possible?p=1161091#post1161091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire melds quite well with the Demon: the Fallen setting because of the common Christian theme, so I'd assume that the Baali hell <i>is </i>the DtF hell.<br /> <br /> Mages do summon some demons from somewhere and especially the Order of Hermes have quite the story about infernalism, but it's unclear whether the place is Malfeas or not. Still, Malfeas is a Middle Umbra realm so I'd call it the closest manifestation of Hell, but not really where the true devils are locked in; I think that a True Hell would be in the Deep Umbra, at the very least.<br /> <br /> That said, Mages are probably able to travel there <i>somehow</i>. But the &quot;how&quot; may very well require Spirit or Forces 9 and enough power to shatter God's will and rewrite the rules of the whole circle of reincarnation.</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as Demon and Vampire share themes, if we assume cross-over with all lines then there are still other possibilities. The Baali would certainly <i>believe</i> they're always dealing with true devils, but they don't have the means to even know the distinction. And the very distinction wouldn't be clear. Just because the Fallen are true Demons, it doesn't mean they are the only ones who can claim the title. What is a Demon? What makes something a Demon? How that works in a fractured universe? The answer isn't simple, and maybe truth is only in the eye of the beholder.<br /> <br /> Of course, any storyteller can settle things straight in a chronicle. I would do that somehow if a player wanted to try the trip. But I'm not seeing a simple answer neither as realistic or interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T02:13:18-08:00","id":1162662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156337-travelling-to-the-abyss-it-is-possible?p=1161147#post1161147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as Demon and Vampire share themes, if we assume cross-over with all lines then there are still other possibilities. The Baali would certainly <i>believe</i> they're always dealing with true devils, but they don't have the means to even know the distinction. And the very distinction wouldn't be clear. Just because the Fallen are true Demons, it doesn't mean they are the only ones who can claim the title. What is a Demon? What makes something a Demon? How that works in a fractured universe? The answer isn't simple, and maybe truth is only in the eye of the beholder.<br /> <br /> Of course, any storyteller can settle things straight in a chronicle. I would do that somehow if a player wanted to try the trip. But I'm not seeing a simple answer neither as realistic or interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> a &quot;true&quot; demon is basically an outsider, instead of a &quot;local&quot; umbrood. Demons are, essentially the same class of being as God/ YHWH/ the demiurge/ etc. they are beings of near absolute power who need faith to manifest it. umbrood don't. that's the difference","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T02:13:18-08:00","id":1162663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156337-travelling-to-the-abyss-it-is-possible?p=1161147#post1161147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as Demon and Vampire share themes, if we assume cross-over with all lines then there are still other possibilities. The Baali would certainly <i>believe</i> they're always dealing with true devils, but they don't have the means to even know the distinction. And the very distinction wouldn't be clear. Just because the Fallen are true Demons, it doesn't mean they are the only ones who can claim the title. What is a Demon? What makes something a Demon? How that works in a fractured universe? The answer isn't simple, and maybe truth is only in the eye of the beholder.<br /> <br /> Of course, any storyteller can settle things straight in a chronicle. I would do that somehow if a player wanted to try the trip. But I'm not seeing a simple answer neither as realistic or interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> a &quot;true&quot; demon is basically an outsider, instead of a &quot;local&quot; umbrood. Demons are, essentially the same class of being as God/ YHWH/ the demiurge/ etc. they are beings of near absolute power who need faith to manifest it. umbrood don't. that's the difference","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-26T17:00:31-08:00","id":1162827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156337-travelling-to-the-abyss-it-is-possible?p=1162663#post1162663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a &quot;true&quot; demon is basically an outsider, instead of a &quot;local&quot; umbrood. Demons are, essentially the same class of being as God/ YHWH/ the demiurge/ etc. they are beings of near absolute power who need faith to manifest it. umbrood don't. that's the difference</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's just one way of looking at it. Who said a local umbrood can't be a demon? On a lot of views demons are local spirits of some sort. On most of Europe and Middle East demons were saw as elemental beings with specific alignment, like the Ifrit and other Jinn. Some on the medieval Catholic Church believed Demons to be on the same class as God, but others thought of it as blasphemy. &quot;Near absolute power&quot; is such a loose term that a Nexus Crawler can easily fit in, and lesser spirits can do with some effort. And faith being a requirement is pretty much a recent school of thought.<br /> <br /> The setting isn't less muddy on this than real life. Lots of spirits describe and comprehend themselves as Demons, they have a huge variety of powers, origins, natures. And the very word &quot;Demon&quot; do not have strict meaning. Also, the setting is heavily defined by particular unreliable narrators. The Fallen have just a narrative of what happened, and few proof of such narrative. The Baali are just denizens of the world, so they calling their patrons &quot;demons&quot; means nearly nothing outside that the Baali themselves believed so. And they could as much miss something as disagree with any given definition for Demon.<br /> <br /> You should first define clearly what is a Demon before you could distinguish objectively what is and what is not a demon. And even then, that would be just the beginning of the discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-27T21:48:10-08:00","id":1163166,"title":"","content":"To go into this discussion, I must assume that the demons in your game are the demons from DEMON THE FALLEN and not umbrood. If you are using demons as umbroods, you gotta diferentiate. These two metaphysics must be tinkered with or adapted, or else it won't work.<br /> So, let's play with metaphisics and paradigm a little bit. I want you to think about your question and about the nature of demon and reality. First, the most important point<br /> <br /> WHAT IS THE ABYSS IN DEMON THE FALLEN?<br /> The demon series answers this as a place OUTSIDE of creation. In houses of the fallen, for example, it is stated how reality was created and it was created by the angels, siphoning the power of the Singer, trough the divine plan that was given to Lucifer. So, reality was made trough blueprints, basically, these blueprints make the tellurian. Not the outside of the tellurian, yes? But they make reality.<br /> So, the question you are making is 'can the spheres let me affect something from OUTSIDE reality?'<br /> There are many answers to this. The Gilgul rite indicates one of them. Avatars aren't spirits. Yet they are affected by the spirit sphere when one uses gilgul to shatter them. How is this possible? Think of it like this - the spheres are just an way to understand reality. Nothing more. Really nothing more. They are a paradigm by which the mage operates. By affecting a certain part of reality you can affect another - and this knowledge touchs the 'WHOLE' but isn't the whole - it is an unnefective tool to descibre the whole(Reffering to the spheres). So, it is more like a ball in a game of billiard. You hit a ball then hit another with that ball. You use sphere to affect something, but due to the characteristics of reality being much bigger than the paradigm that encompasses the spheres, it hits 'another' part of reality that isn't described by them AT ALL.<br /> Does that makes sense or help in any way?<br /> <br /> Also, the abyss from werewolf isn't the same abyss. The abyss from demon the fallen is beneath the shadowland. Assuming demon metaphysics, it wouldn't be the abyss from the lasombra as well. WHY? Because there isn't ANY reality concepts in the abyss from demon. In the abyss of lasombra there is still FORM. And form is a concept from reality, built by the angels of DE LORD~~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23536-schrodingoethe","name":"Schrodingoethe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T07:35:06-08:00","id":1163224,"title":"","content":"For instance. The Abyss of Werewolf certainly isn't depicted as a place of nothingness, but if you go down trough that Abyss you reach a point of sensory deprivation-and then you can go further down. No one, not even a Celestine-level being can go to the bottom and return, so you can argue that either the Lasombra or the Demon Abyss can be accessed from there. Demons haven't escaped trough the Middle Umbra but that may be because the phenomena that craked the doors of Hell don't happened there, there the Wards are more or less intact (making it notably easier to get in than to get out).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-28-2017, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T08:53:14-08:00","id":1163253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156337-travelling-to-the-abyss-it-is-possible?p=1162827#post1162827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that's just one way of looking at it. Who said a local umbrood can't be a demon? On a lot of views demons are local spirits of some sort. On most of Europe and Middle East demons were saw as elemental beings with specific alignment, like the Ifrit and other Jinn. Some on the medieval Catholic Church believed Demons to be on the same class as God, but others thought of it as blasphemy. &quot;Near absolute power&quot; is such a loose term that a Nexus Crawler can easily fit in, and lesser spirits can do with some effort. And faith being a requirement is pretty much a recent school of thought.<br /> <br /> The setting isn't less muddy on this than real life. Lots of spirits describe and comprehend themselves as Demons, they have a huge variety of powers, origins, natures. And the very word &quot;Demon&quot; do not have strict meaning. Also, the setting is heavily defined by particular unreliable narrators. The Fallen have just a narrative of what happened, and few proof of such narrative. The Baali are just denizens of the world, so they calling their patrons &quot;demons&quot; means nearly nothing outside that the Baali themselves believed so. And they could as much miss something as disagree with any given definition for Demon.<br /> <br /> You should first define clearly what is a Demon before you could distinguish objectively what is and what is not a demon. And even then, that would be just the beginning of the discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, that's why i said TRUE Demon. other beings can definetely be demons in the sense that they are inimical to humanity's interests and of course the average demonologist/infernalist won't know the difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T15:11:26-08:00","id":1163348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156337-travelling-to-the-abyss-it-is-possible?p=1163224#post1163224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance. The Abyss of Werewolf certainly isn't depicted as a place of nothingness, but if you go down trough that Abyss you reach a point of sensory deprivation-and then you can go further down. No one, not even a Celestine-level being can go to the bottom and return, so you can argue that either the Lasombra or the Demon Abyss can be accessed from there. Demons haven't escaped trough the Middle Umbra but that may be because the phenomena that craked the doors of Hell don't happened there, there the Wards are more or less intact (making it notably easier to get in than to get out).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with any assertion that they didn't escaped through the Middle Umbra. Not that I'm saying they did, but it seems as much a possibility as anything else AFAIK. Demon line don't bother much in defining the spirit realms, and other lines aren't reliably to tell anything about DtF. Even assuming they were, until the last canonical narrative Demons were still too far apart for their exodus to be easily witnessed <u>and</u> recognized by others. Even for experienced umbral travelers they would easily be taken for other denizens of those realms. Demons only find one another easily because they have the means to do so at ease. Like supernatural senses with a radius of miles fresh out of Hell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156337-travelling-to-the-abyss-it-is-possible?p=1163253#post1163253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well, that's why i said TRUE Demon. other beings can definetely be demons in the sense that they are inimical to humanity's interests and of course the average demonologist/infernalist won't know the difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant was that even this assertion isn't entirely true. Since there is no strict definition for Demon, the Fallen can't claim the title more than other spirits. And since their claims can't be proved for sure, you can't take it at face value even if you assume their definition as true.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is semantics, and only mean something if you want to. If your game assumes their narrative as mostly true, as mine do, then they are pretty much &quot;true demons&quot;. But it isn't a default for the entire WoD (yet).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T22:38:19-08:00","id":1168129,"title":"","content":"the location of the demons abyss is in the shadowlands- this is mentioned many times in both the core book and in supplemental materials such as the storytellers handbook and the earthbound book. it is also worth mentioning that it was the void Engineers dicking around in the Labyrinth with a nuke that ultimately cracked the gates of hell and set the demons free. thats mentioned in Ends of Empire i believe. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>there are no bad ideas, just ideas that have not been refined enough","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1608-iamthesweeper","name":"IAmTheSweeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}